# Every text file has LF line ends in the repository and in every checkout, whatever
# `core.autocrlf` says (Git for Windows sets it to true and would check them out with CRLF).
# The checks read files from disk and compare them byte by byte with what the code makes or
# with a recorded hash, and the shell scripts must run in Git Bash.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Verbatim copies of sources kept outside the repo. The bytes of the Chroma Lab distribution
# are pinned by a manifest (app/src/ui/chroma/snapshot.json) that the Vite config checks before
# anything else: nothing may convert them.
app/src/data/** -text

# Never text, whatever their first bytes look like.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.m4a binary
*.wav binary
*.webm binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.wasm binary
*.pdf binary
